From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CADCraft <noreply@cadcraft.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:47:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(fonts): make the bundled fallback faces a feature

slab-fonts compiled Inter and JetBrains Mono (eight files, 2.77 MB, SIL OFL
1.1) into every binary and wasm module that links the kernel, with no way to
leave them out. A host that paints with faces of its own (a web page with its
own font stack, an application that may not redistribute fonts) had to ship
them anyway.

`bundled-fonts` is a new feature of slab-fonts, on by default and forwarded by
every crate that links it, so nothing changes for a default build. The
workspace now inherits its own crates without default features;
`--no-default-features` on the crate being built gives a build with no font
bytes in it. slab-cli and slab-wasm forward `wc-embed` the same way.

Without the feature:

- `slab_fonts::asset` returns `None` (it now returns an `Option`) and
  `FONT_ASSETS` is empty.
- A family with no compile-time bytes is compiled to FONT tables made from
  `slab_fonts::default_metrics`: a small designed advance model (a fixed
  advance for a monospaced class, six width classes for a proportional one),
  documented in the crate and derived from no font file. The tables carry no
  data, so the kernel lays their text out unshaped from the table's own
  advances, the path it already takes for a host-owned runtime face.
- The kernel reports, once per family, a `font-default` frame diagnostic
  naming each family whose text was laid out from such a table. A family the
  host registers (`inst_font_register`, metrics alone or with bytes) resolves
  to the runtime table and is not reported.
- The compiler does not check glyph coverage for a family it has no face for.
- SVG and terminal cells need metrics only and work unchanged; the SVG has no
  `@font-face` to embed. A raster export (PNG, APNG) of text with no outlines
  available returns an error naming the family
  (`slab_compile::render::missing_face`) instead of a picture without the
  text; it paints once the host registers the face's bytes.

Tests: the suites pass in both configurations. Tests that need a bundled face
are gated on the feature; `tests/fontless.rs` covers the build without it.
The conformance goldens are measured with the bundled faces and hold only in
the default configuration.
